OL,3,AKing acknowledges 'suffering of the
OL,4,Apast' as Caribbean tour begins
OL,5,
OL,6,FKing Charles III has begun his tour of
OL,7,Fthe Caribbean by acknowledging the
OL,8,F"great suffering of the past" as he
OL,9,Ffaced calls for slavery reparations.
OL,11,FSpeaking an event in the Bahamas
OL,12,Fcelebrating local youth, the King said
OL,13,Fthe country's culture was "born out of
OL,14,Fdarkness", and it was "only right" to
OL,15,Facknowledge historic injustices.
OL,17,FHis nine-day tour will culminate in the
OL,18,FCommonwealth Heads of Government
OL,19,FMeeting (CHOGM), where the King has
OL,20,Fconfirmed leaders will discuss the
OL,21,Fregion's legacy of slavery.
OL,23,APub: 27-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG7/39
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
